{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AZoXdL8DcrsELPYD8RGn4Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. This project derives specifications from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `docs/` (specs), `cmd/` (utility implementations), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets).\n\n**Current State**: `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` exists in source code (confirmed). All other packages have code at generation-merged tags but not on the working branch. Specs are complete for releases 00.0 through 04.1 (foundational infra, cat, sponge, du, wc, ls). Releases 02.0–02.2 have pending specs.\n\n**Current Release**: Release 00.0 (Batch 0 — foundational infrastructure) is the earliest incomplete release with 4 use cases: magefiles (excluded from generation per DD7), format, sys, testutils.\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nRelease 00.0 is the target. `pkg/testutils` implementation exists (source_code confirms `difftest.go`). Per P8 ordering, tests follow implementation. The next task is tests for the existing `pkg/testutils` RunDiffTests, anchored to prd001 R2.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4 (core comparison logic).\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Test pkg/testutils RunDiffTests core comparison (prd001 R2.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml (requirements R2.1, R3.2, R3.3, R3.4, R3.6)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (existing RunDiffTests implementation to verify)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for RunDiffTests core comparison -- stdout, stderr, exit code\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test prd001 R2.1: RunDiffTests executes both goBinary and refBinary with identical args, stdin, env, and working directory, capturing their outputs independently\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test prd001 R3.2: RunDiffTests passes when both binaries produce identical stdout and reports divergence with expected format when stdout differs\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test prd001 R3.3: RunDiffTests passes when both binaries produce identical stderr and reports divergence with expected format when stderr differs\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test prd001 R3.4: RunDiffTests passes when both binaries return the same exit code and reports divergence when exit codes differ\"\n      - id: R5\n        text: \"Build minimal Go test helper programs (compiled to temporary directories) that produce controlled stdout, stderr, and exit codes for use as goBinary and refBinary inputs to RunDiffTests\"\n      - id: R6\n        text: \"Test both the matching case (no divergence) and the divergent case for each comparison dimension\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"RunDiffTests accepts binary paths per ARCHITECTURE.yaml. Test helpers are small main() programs compiled with go build to t.TempDir(), producing known output so tests are deterministic.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Per prd001 R3.6, each DiffTest runs as a named subtest via t.Run. Tests verify this by using distinct DiffTest.Name values.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Test file follows project naming convention from ARCHITECTURE.yaml: test files mirror source, so difftest.go becomes difftest_test.go.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/testutils/difftest_test.go exists and compiles without errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/testutils/... passes with all tests green\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"At least one test verifies RunDiffTests passes when both binaries produce identical stdout, stderr, and exit code\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"At least one test verifies RunDiffTests detects stdout divergence between binaries\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"At least one test verifies RunDiffTests detects stderr divergence between binaries\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"At least one test verifies RunDiffTests detects exit code divergence between binaries\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20291,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20291},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f8201c83-a947-4bf2-a083-bffda405dd18","uuid":"57c2d39d-e648-45da-a11a-df2d6ef04208"}
